					<description><![CDATA[When her genius grandfather dies, Alexa Martin&#8217;s simple life is changed immeasurably, taking her from a humble history scholar to owner of a cutting-edge technology and research company. Along with the smartest and brightest of her university friends they embark &#8230; <a href="https://rodyne.com/?p=2032">Continue reading <span class="meta-nav">&#8594;</span></a>]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="has-light-gray-background-color has-background wp-block-paragraph">When her genius grandfather dies, Alexa Martin&#8217;s simple life is changed immeasurably, taking her from a humble history scholar to owner of a cutting-edge technology and research company. Along with the smartest and brightest of her university friends they embark to push two scientific breakthroughs which will hopefully start the world on a path of recovery from its current precarious future. However, both breakthroughs have the ability to massively disrupt current industries, and with the world and a host of powerful governments and interest groups watching she needs to tread especially carefully.</p>



<div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-8f761849 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow" style="flex-basis:33.33%">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><a href="https://books2read.com/u/bxxjJe" target="_blank" rel=" noreferrer noopener"><img decoding="async" width="337" height="495" src="https://rodyne.com/wp-content/uploads/The-Phoney-War.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-2036" srcset="https://rodyne.com/wp-content/uploads/The-Phoney-War.jpg 337w, https://rodyne.com/wp-content/uploads/The-Phoney-War-204x300.jpg 204w" sizes="(max-width: 337px) 100vw, 337px" /></a></figure>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow" style="flex-basis:66.66%">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The first book in the trilogy focuses on the introduction of the main characters, the science and technology, and sets the foundations for the later more action-packed books. It can be read completely stand-alone and has no sex or violence so is safe for any age. The book does dwell a bit on the science and technology which while not important to the story do make it a more fun read if you understand them.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">November 2025 Update: The whole book series is now available as a free eBook download. Click the book link in the menu to the right to download..</p>
</div>
</div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The 130,000 word paperback is available at <a href="https://www.amazon.com/Phoney-War-Summer-Reasoning/dp/B0D154R9QB?th=1&amp;psc=1&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.iAGHDL9oQp64vcRk8gN6yZgDuprWePktIemk2JLOidGacEKpLjzlRltBKn-v6vgGOD503PcW0bC8F10NADon4AGRPjBCsZfewTFQFG7a7hk.cwkSn8IKmkm9dVg9B30S0wPLBLHpsj8i2xBXoYaZtbU&amp;dib_tag=AUTHOR" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Amazon</a></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Cover Design Refresh</span></p>



<div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-8f761849 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The new cover designs for the other two paperback books are also awesome in my humble opinion. The first one you have already seen, and if you&#8217;ve read the whole series you should be able to visualise the chapters which all of these come from. </p>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><a href="https://rodyne.com/?p=2450"><img decoding="async" width="400" height="600" src="https://rodyne.com/wp-content/uploads/singularity.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-2037" srcset="https://rodyne.com/wp-content/uploads/singularity.jpg 400w, https://rodyne.com/wp-content/uploads/singularity-200x300.jpg 200w" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" /></a></figure>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><a href="https://rodyne.com/?p=2457"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="256" height="348" src="https://rodyne.com/wp-content/uploads/End-Game.png" alt="" class="wp-image-2038" srcset="https://rodyne.com/wp-content/uploads/End-Game.png 256w, https://rodyne.com/wp-content/uploads/End-Game-221x300.png 221w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 256px) 100vw, 256px" /></a></figure>
</div>
</div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The 5.5 x 8.5 (15.24cm x 22.9cm) Book format with the off-white pages is the most esthetically pleasing. The bigger 9&#215;6 format I have available at Amazon has less pages and a few cents cheaper to print but feel a little cheap, but it is all semantic, at $20+ per book I don&#8217;t expect the market to be anyone but me, which I will buy to go to friends and eventually the local libraries.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Oh, on a final note, I gave a copy of the paperback version of A Level of Consciousness to the <a href="https://www.marlboroughlibraries.govt.nz/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Blenheim library</a>, it is one of the ones with the original cover, so if you live in the area, pop in and <a href="https://ent.kotui.org.nz/client/en_AU/marlborough/search/detailnonmodal/ent:$002f$002fSD_ILS$002f0$002fSD_ILS:5827025/one" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">reserve</a> it for free. I will also donate them the three paperbacks above once I am happy with the quality, a big thank you again to the <a href="https://natlib.govt.nz/publishers-and-authors/isbns-issns-and-ismns" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">National Library of NZ </a>for giving me another 10 ISBN numbers, it should take me a few years to use them up.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">For more information on The Summer of Reasoning, click <a href="https://rodyne.com/?p=1252">here..</a></p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
